# Hindsight 官方镜像 v1.3.0 配置参考（所有赋值均已注释，直接使用本文件不会启用配置）
# 使用：复制为 .env，阅读每组说明，只对需要的条目取消行首的 #，并替换占位符。
# 同一变量可能在多个 provider 示例中出现；只能选择一个有效赋值，不能把全部示例取消注释。
# 当前 compose.yaml 通过 env_file 加载 .env；environment 中的插值项/默认值会覆盖 env_file。
# 当前本地 compose 默认 Ollama、host.docker.internal:11434/v1、minicpm5-2b:latest，
# LLM_MAX_CONCURRENT=1、OLLAMA_NUM_CTX=32768、RETAIN_MAX_COMPLETION_TOKENS=16000、WORKER_ID=hindsight-local；
# 以下保留的是上游官方示例，不表示这些本地 compose 默认值发生变化。
# 切换 LLM provider 时还须按需覆盖 LLM_MODEL 和 LLM_BASE_URL；否则仍沿用本地 Ollama 默认值。
# .env 中所有取消注释的条目都会传入容器；shell 变量只覆盖 compose.yaml 中显式插值的条目。
# 英文说明保留 v1.3.0 原文，避免数百项翻译改变含义。示例值 != 默认值。
# “默认（官方文档）”记录文档原文；空赋值只是填写位置，不等于“不设置”，通常应保持注释。
# 安全：.env 可能包含密钥，不要提交版本库或分享；限制文件读取权限。
# 所有 API key/token/secret/password 示例均非本机凭证。不要把生产数据、访问令牌或日志暴露到公网。
# 默认 API 未启用鉴权；公开访问前配置 TENANT_EXTENSION + TENANT_API_KEY，CP 单独设置 ACCESS_KEY。
# 数据库连接串也可能含密码；外部模型会收到记忆内容，日志/trace/debug 可能记录敏感输入输出。
# 容器内 localhost 指容器自身；访问 macOS 宿主服务可使用 host.docker.internal。
# 仅改 .env 不会修改端口映射、挂载、安装 extras 或镜像构建参数；应用配置需要重建容器而非只 restart。
# 依赖：部分 provider/扩展需额外依赖、凭证文件挂载或自定义镜像；列出变量不承诺官方镜像全都内置。
# 官方 Dockerfile 明确不包含 local-onnx extra；NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH 是构建参数，不是此镜像的运行时开关。
# 来源（固定版本）：
# https://github.com/vectorize-io/hindsight/blob/v1.3.0/.env.example
# https://github.com/vectorize-io/hindsight/blob/v1.3.0/hindsight-docs/docs/developer/configuration.mdx
# https://github.com/vectorize-io/hindsight/blob/v1.3.0/hindsight-api-slim/hindsight_api/config.py
# https://github.com/vectorize-io/hindsight/blob/v1.3.0/docker/standalone/start-all.sh
# https://github.com/vectorize-io/hindsight/blob/v1.3.0/docker/standalone/Dockerfile
# 范围：上游样例 + 文档静态变量表 + config.py 补充 + 镜像启动变量；动态前缀用具体例子。



# LLM Configuration (Required)
# Supported providers: openai, openai-responses, groq, ollama, gemini, anthropic, lmstudio, vertexai, minimax, deepseek, zai, atlas, meta, volcano, openai-codex, claude-code, cursor, antigravity, github-copilot
# Provider: `openai`, `openai-responses`, `openai-codex`, `chatgpt`, `claude-code`, `cursor`, `antigravity`,
# `github-copilot`, `anthropic`, `gemini`, `groq`, `minimax`, `deepseek`, `zai`, `opencode-go`, `meta`, `nous`,
# `xai-oauth`, `fireworks`, `ollama`, `ollama-cloud`, `lmstudio`, `llamacpp`, `vertexai`, `bedrock`, `litellm`,
# `litellmrouter`, `volcano`, `openrouter`, `requesty`, `none`, or `package.module:ClassName` for a [custom
# provider](./extensions.md#custom-llm-provider)
# 默认（官方文档）：`openai`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# API key for providers that require one; unused by `github-copilot`. Optional for `anthropic` when [Workload
# Identity Federation](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/manage-claude/workload-identity-federation) is configured
# (see the Anthropic example below)
# 默认（官方文档）：-；下一行为上游示例值。
# 安全：敏感凭证占位符；请替换并保护 .env，勿提交或公开。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_API_KEY=your-api-key-here
# Model name
# 默认（官方文档）：`gpt-5-mini`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# Custom LLM endpoint
# 默认（官方文档）：Provider default；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# Vision slot — the model used for retain chunks that carry an inline attachment.
# Only those chunks use it; every text-only chunk stays on the retain LLM, so a
# bank ingesting the occasional screenshot need not run (or pay for) a vision
# model on all of its text. Unset, attachments go to the retain LLM as before.
# Provider for the **vision slot** — the model used only for retain chunks that carry an [inline
# attachment](#inline-attachments-in-retain). Every text-only chunk keeps using the retain LLM, so a bank whose
# documents mostly *are* text does not pay a vision model's price for all of it. Unset, attachments go to the retain
# LLM.
# 默认（官方文档）：Retain LLM；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_VLM_PROVIDER=gemini
# API key for the vision slot.
# 默认（官方文档）：Retain LLM's；下一行为上游示例值。
# 安全：敏感凭证占位符；请替换并保护 .env，勿提交或公开。
# HINDSIGHT_API_VLM_API_KEY=your-vision-api-key
# Model for the vision slot. This is the model `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_VISION` and the `422` vision check apply to, since
# it is the one that will actually be handed the attachment.
# 默认（官方文档）：Retain LLM's；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_VLM_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# Base URL for the vision slot. Follows `HINDSIGHT_API_VLM_PROVIDER`'s own default when that is set and this is not —
# it never inherits the retain provider's host, which would send the request to the wrong endpoint with the wrong
# key.
# 默认（官方文档）：Provider default；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_VLM_BASE_URL=
# Each of these overrides its HINDSIGHT_API_RETAIN_LLM_* value for the vision slot
# (used only when the slot is configured above), e.g. a low reasoning level for images.
# Reasoning effort for the vision slot. Lets a cheap extraction model run at `xhigh` while the vision model runs at
# `low`. Like the rows below, it applies only once the vision slot is configured by one of the four settings above.
# 默认（官方文档）：Retain LLM's；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_VLM_REASONING_EFFORT=low
# Extra request body (JSON) for the vision slot.
# 默认（官方文档）：Retain LLM's；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_VLM_EXTRA_BODY=
# Cache affinity for the vision slot.
# 默认（官方文档）：Retain LLM's；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_VLM_CACHE_AFFINITY=
# Timeout for vision slot requests (seconds).
# 默认（官方文档）：Retain LLM's；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_VLM_TIMEOUT=
# Max retries for vision slot requests.
# 默认（官方文档）：Retain LLM's；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_VLM_MAX_RETRIES=
# Initial retry backoff for the vision slot (seconds).
# 默认（官方文档）：Retain LLM's；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_VLM_INITIAL_BACKOFF=
# Max retry backoff for the vision slot (seconds).
# 默认（官方文档）：Retain LLM's；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_VLM_MAX_BACKOFF=
# Reasoning effort for providers/models that support it. Examples: none, low, medium, high, xhigh.
# Set it and the value is sent as given, whatever the model is called — use `none` to stop a
# self-hosted reasoning model (vLLM, Ollama, llama.cpp, TGI) emitting thinking blocks. Unset,
# no reasoning parameter is sent at all and each model runs at its own default effort.
# Reasoning effort for providers/models that support it (for example `none`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`). Set
# it and the value is sent as given, whatever your model is called — which is how you control thinking-token volume
# on a self-hosted reasoning model (vLLM, Ollama, llama.cpp, TGI), where `none` is often the only value that removes
# the thinking block. Leave it unset and no reasoning parameter is sent at all, so each model runs at its own default
# effort. Honoured by `openai` and every OpenAI-compatible provider, `openai-responses`, `chatgpt`, `openai-codex`,
# `xai`, `llamacpp`, and `litellm`/`litellmrouter` (which translate it per target provider). `claude-code` passes
# `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh` or `max` to each operation's CLI (other values are ignored with a warning). The
# native `gemini`/`vertexai`, `anthropic`, `cursor` and `antigravity` providers have no reasoning-effort control and
# log a warning at startup if you set one — reach those models through `litellm` to apply it.
# 默认（官方文档）：Unset (model's own default)；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_REASONING_EFFORT=low

# Sampling temperature for internal LLM calls. Set a number in [0.0, 2.0], or `none`
# to omit the temperature parameter entirely (required for models that reject explicit
# temperatures, e.g. Azure gpt-5.5). The global override below applies to every operation;
# per-operation overrides (defaults: verification=0.0, retain=0.1, reflect=0.9,
# consolidation=0.0) take precedence. The mental-model refresh's delta and retraction
# calls follow consolidation unless HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TEMPERATURE_MENTAL_MODEL_REFRESH is set.
# Global override for the sampling temperature of internal LLM calls. Set a number in `[0.0, 2.0]`, or `none` (also
# `default`/`off`/empty) to **omit** the temperature parameter entirely — required for models that reject explicit
# temperatures, e.g. Azure `gpt-5.5`, which only accepts its default value. Per-operation variables below override
# this.
# 默认（官方文档）：Per-operation defaults；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TEMPERATURE=none
# Temperature for the startup connection check. Number in `[0.0, 2.0]` or `none` to omit. Overrides
# `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TEMPERATURE`.
# 默认（官方文档）：`0.0`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TEMPERATURE_VERIFICATION=0.0
# Temperature for fact extraction during retain. Number in `[0.0, 2.0]` or `none` to omit. Overrides
# `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TEMPERATURE`.
# 默认（官方文档）：`0.1`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TEMPERATURE_RETAIN=0.1
# Temperature for the reflect "thinking" step. Number in `[0.0, 2.0]` or `none` to omit. Overrides
# `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TEMPERATURE`.
# 默认（官方文档）：`0.9`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TEMPERATURE_REFLECT=0.9
# Temperature for consolidation (dedup), and for the mental-model refresh's delta and retraction calls unless
# `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TEMPERATURE_MENTAL_MODEL_REFRESH` is set. Number in `[0.0, 2.0]` or `none` to omit. Overrides
# `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TEMPERATURE`.
# 默认（官方文档）：`0.0`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TEMPERATURE_CONSOLIDATION=0.0
# Temperature for the mental-model refresh's structured edit calls (delta and retraction). Number in `[0.0, 2.0]` or
# `none` to omit. Set it when the refresh runs its own model (`HINDSIGHT_API_MENTAL_MODEL_REFRESH_LLM_*`) whose
# recommended temperature differs from consolidation's.
# 默认（官方文档）：Falls back to `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TEMPERATURE_CONSOLIDATION`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TEMPERATURE_MENTAL_MODEL_REFRESH=0.0

# Grammar-enforce structured output (json_schema strict) instead of the soft
# schema-in-prompt path. Helps weaker self-hosted models that emit prose preambles
# or invalid JSON. The global override below applies to every operation;
# per-operation overrides take precedence, in both directions -- set one to false
# to opt that operation out while the global flag is on.
# Grammar-enforce structured output via `json_schema` `strict: true` instead of the soft "schema-in-prompt +
# `json_object`" path. Typed Pydantic response models are serialized directly into the OpenAI strict subset: every
# object rejects additional properties, every declared property is required, and nullable fields remain nullable. Use
# it with weaker self-hosted models that return prose preambles, markdown ` ```json ` fences, or invalid JSON — which
# otherwise fail to parse and wedge retain/consolidation. Applies to OpenAI-compatible backends (OpenAI, LM Studio,
# Ollama, Volcano, llama.cpp, vLLM), Codex, and LiteLLM; Gemini already enforces its native `response_schema`
# regardless, and providers without a strict mode ignore it. LM Studio, Ollama, and Volcano are the most common
# cases: their soft path skips even `json_object` mode (they don't honor it reliably), so a small model's raw output
# goes unconstrained — enabling this flag is the fix for a `JSONDecodeError` during retain on those backends.
# 默认（官方文档）：`false`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_STRICT_SCHEMA=false
# Override `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_STRICT_SCHEMA` for retain (fact extraction) only. Applies to both the streaming and
# batch extraction paths.
# 默认（官方文档）：Inherits global；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_STRICT_SCHEMA_RETAIN=true
# Override `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_STRICT_SCHEMA` for every reflect step: the structured-output extraction, a mental
# model's delta-refresh operations, and the tool turns (each search turn and the closing answer). The tool turns are
# held to the schema unless this is set to `false`; the global flag does not reach them. Set it to `false` for a
# model that runs away under the grammar (writes whitespace or repeats itself until the token limit or a timeout).
# 默认（官方文档）：Inherits global (tool turns: `true`)；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_STRICT_SCHEMA_REFLECT=true  # also reflect's tool turns, which stay strict unless this is false
# Override `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_STRICT_SCHEMA` for consolidation only (both the batch consolidation call and
# observation dedup).
# 默认（官方文档）：Inherits global；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_STRICT_SCHEMA_CONSOLIDATION=true
# Ceiling on the connect phase (TCP + TLS handshake) of an LLM request, in seconds.
# Read, write and pool keep the full HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TIMEOUT budget, so an unreachable
# endpoint fails fast instead of burning the whole request timeout. 0 disables the cap.
# Ceiling on the **connect** phase (TCP + TLS handshake) of an LLM request, in seconds. The read, write and pool
# phases keep the full `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TIMEOUT` budget; capping connect separately means an unreachable or wedged
# endpoint fails in seconds instead of consuming the whole request timeout. Effective value is the smaller of this
# and the request timeout. Set to `0` to disable the cap and use one value across all four phases. Applies to every
# provider whose HTTP client Hindsight constructs (all OpenAI-compatible backends, `openai-responses`, `chatgpt`,
# `anthropic`, `openai-codex`, `xai-oauth`, `fireworks`, `nous`, `llamacpp`); `litellm`/`litellmrouter` and
# `gemini`/`vertexai` own their transports and take a single total deadline instead, and
# `claude-code`/`cursor`/`antigravity`/`github-copilot` drive a CLI rather than a socket.
# 默认（官方文档）：`10`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_CONNECT_TIMEOUT=10

# Log level for the httpx/httpcore loggers. DEBUG traces every LLM request through its
# transport phases (connect_tcp, send_request_headers, receive_response_headers), which
# is how you tell a request that stalled before being sent from one never answered.
# Log level for the `httpx` and `httpcore` loggers. Set to `DEBUG` to trace each LLM request through its transport
# phases (`connect_tcp`, `send_request_headers`, `receive_response_headers`) — the way to tell a request that stalled
# before it was ever sent from one that was sent and never answered. Verbose; for diagnosis only.
# 默认（官方文档）：`WARNING`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_HTTP_LOG_LEVEL=WARNING

# Whether the backend honours response_format json_object. Unset = provider decides
# (no for lmstudio/ollama/volcano, yes otherwise). Set false for provider=openai
# pointed at a local server that can't constrain output: the schema then goes in
# the prompt only.
# Whether the OpenAI-compatible backend honours `response_format={"type": "json_object"}` on the soft (non-strict)
# structured-output path. Leave unset and the provider decides: LM Studio, Ollama, Volcano and z.ai get the schema in
# the prompt only, llama.cpp follows `HINDSIGHT_API_LLAMACPP_NO_GRAMMAR`, and every other provider also sends
# `json_object`. z.ai is skipped because its `json_object` mode deletes the literal token `json` from the generated
# text, so `latest.json` comes back as `latest.` — valid JSON, silently corrupted. Set `false` for `provider=openai`
# pointed at a local server that can't constrain output: some such servers rewrite the prompt instead, and a thinking
# model can loop on the rewrite until the LLM timeout. This doesn't make a model write JSON. It only drops the
# request the server mishandles, so the model still has to follow the schema in the prompt. Set `true` to force
# `json_object` on a backend that would otherwise skip it.
# 默认（官方文档）：Provider decides；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_JSON_MODE=
# On that path, have the backend enforce the response schema itself instead of
# json_object (any JSON object). For vLLM / llama.cpp; set true for Gemma 4 on vLLM.
# When the OpenAI-compatible soft path sends a response format, send the response schema itself (`{"type":
# "json_schema", "strict": false}`) instead of `json_object`, which only promises some JSON object. The schema stays
# in the prompt too, so the model also writes the optional fields a grammar does not force. For backends that
# grammar-constrain any schema, such as vLLM and llama.cpp. Set `true` for Gemma 4 on vLLM: under `json_object` it
# answered retain with schema keys echoed back or an empty facts list, and on long nested replies (mental model
# refresh, consolidation) closed the list early and repeated keys until the token cap. This is not
# `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_STRICT_SCHEMA`, which sends a rewritten schema with every field required.
# 默认（官方文档）：`false`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_ENFORCE_SCHEMA=false
# JSON_MODE for retain's fact extraction only (unset = the global value). Set false
# for Gemma 4 on vLLM: constrained, it answers retain with an empty facts list.
# `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_JSON_MODE` for retain's fact extraction only; unset, retain follows the global
# value. `false` also turns off schema enforcement for retain, leaving the schema in the prompt. Set `false` for
# Gemma 4 on vLLM: retain is the one answer that may legally be empty, and under any decoding constraint
# (`json_object` or the enforced schema) Gemma answered content full of facts with `{"facts": []}`, while
# unconstrained it did not. The cause is vLLM's `--structured-outputs-config.disable_any_whitespace`, which blocks
# the newline Gemma writes after the list opens; allowing whitespace instead brings back replies that loop on
# whitespace.
# 默认（官方文档）：Global value；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_RETAIN_LLM_OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_JSON_MODE=

# Constrain retain's occurred_start/occurred_end to an ISO timestamp with a JSON
# Schema pattern. Stops grammar-constrained models reasoning inside the timestamp
# string and burning the whole completion budget. Off by default: backends that
# validate schemas against an allowlist (Bedrock) reject the keyword with a 400.
# Whether the LLM backend accepts JSON Schema `pattern` in structured-output schemas. When `true`, retain constrains
# `occurred_start` / `occurred_end` to an ISO timestamp, which stops a grammar-constrained model from reasoning
# inside the timestamp string — a failure that corrupts the date and can burn the entire completion budget on an
# unterminated response. Left `false` because support is narrow and rejection is a hard 400 at request time: Bedrock
# validates schemas against an allowlist that excludes this keyword, and OpenAI errors on unsupported keywords under
# `strict`. Backends that neither enforce nor reject it gain nothing.
# 默认（官方文档）：`false`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_SUPPORTS_STRING_PATTERN=false

# Pin a conversation to one backend prompt cache (OpenAI-compatible providers only).
# Server-side prompt caches are per backend server, so the same conversation has to
# reach the same one to hit. Values: auto (default), xai_conv_id (sends xAI's
# x-grok-conv-id header), openai_prompt_cache_key (sends OpenAI's prompt_cache_key
# field), none (sends nothing). "auto" picks from the base URL host and is an
# allowlist: x.ai / grok.com get the header, native OpenAI / openai.com / Azure
# OpenAI get the field, and every other backend gets nothing. Per-operation
# overrides take precedence. Set to none to disable entirely.
# Pin a conversation to one backend prompt cache on the OpenAI-compatible providers, Fireworks and Nous. Server-side
# prompt caches are per backend server, so the same conversation has to reach the same one for a cache hit.
# `xai_conv_id` sends xAI's documented `x-grok-conv-id` header; `openai_prompt_cache_key` sends OpenAI's
# `prompt_cache_key` field; `auto` picks one from the configured base URL host (x.ai / grok.com &rarr; `xai_conv_id`;
# native OpenAI or an openai.com host &rarr; `openai_prompt_cache_key`; anything else, including Azure OpenAI, &rarr;
# `none`); `none` sends nothing. The id is the operation's trace id, so every LLM call of one
# retain/reflect/consolidation run shares it. `auto` is an allowlist rather than a best-effort probe, so an unknown
# OpenAI-compatible backend (vLLM, ollama, groq, openrouter, a custom proxy) receives byte-identical requests to
# before; set `none` to disable entirely. Anthropic and Gemini/Vertex do their own caching and ignore this.
# 默认（官方文档）：`auto`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_CACHE_AFFINITY=auto
# Prompt-cache affinity mode for retain operations
# 默认（官方文档）：Falls back to `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_CACHE_AFFINITY`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_RETAIN_LLM_CACHE_AFFINITY=none
# Prompt-cache affinity mode for reflect operations
# 默认（官方文档）：Falls back to `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_CACHE_AFFINITY`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_REFLECT_LLM_CACHE_AFFINITY=xai_conv_id
# Prompt-cache affinity mode for consolidation operations
# 默认（官方文档）：Falls back to `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_CACHE_AFFINITY`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_CONSOLIDATION_LLM_CACHE_AFFINITY=none

# The automatic mental-model refresh runs the reflect pipeline in the background.
# By default it uses the reflect LLM; this group lets it use a different one, which
# matters on a single-GPU box where interactive reflect wants a thinking model but
# the background job wants a fast no-think one that cannot blow the wall timeout or
# starve the interactive stream. Each field falls back to its REFLECT_LLM_*
# counterpart (which falls back to the global LLM_*), except the timeout: refresh
# never inherits REFLECT_LLM_TIMEOUT, it falls back to LLM_TIMEOUT.
# LLM provider for the automatic mental-model refresh
# 默认（官方文档）：Falls back to `HINDSIGHT_API_REFLECT_LLM_PROVIDER`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_MENTAL_MODEL_REFRESH_LLM_PROVIDER=lmstudio
# Model for the automatic refresh
# 默认（官方文档）：Falls back to `HINDSIGHT_API_REFLECT_LLM_MODEL`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_MENTAL_MODEL_REFRESH_LLM_MODEL=qwen3-chat
# Timeout for refresh requests (seconds). Nobody is waiting on a background refresh, so this is usually set much
# higher than the reflect timeout.
# 默认（官方文档）：Falls back to `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_TIMEOUT`, never to `HINDSIGHT_API_REFLECT_LLM_TIMEOUT` (that one is sized
# for a caller waiting on the answer)；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_MENTAL_MODEL_REFRESH_LLM_TIMEOUT=2700
# Extra cap on concurrent refresh LLM requests, composed with the global cap. Unset → only the global cap applies.
# 默认（官方文档）：Unset；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_MENTAL_MODEL_REFRESH_LLM_MAX_CONCURRENT=1

# Give litellm/litellmrouter/bedrock the structured-output schema in the prompt
# instead of response_format. Enable it for backends that reject response_format
# outright -- e.g. Bedrock Claude in ap-southeast-2 ("Extra inputs are not permitted");
# the same model in us-east-1 accepts response_format and needs nothing here.
# Give the LiteLLM-backed providers (`litellm`, `litellmrouter`, `bedrock`) the structured-output schema in the
# prompt, and parse the reply, instead of sending `response_format`. Set to `true` for backends that reject
# `response_format` outright. This is region-dependent on Bedrock Claude: `ap-southeast-2` (`au.*` inference
# profiles) refuses the translated Converse `outputConfig` with `Extra inputs are not permitted`, while the same
# model in `us-east-1` (`us.*`) accepts it and needs nothing here. Verified against both. Other providers ignore it.
# 默认（官方文档）：`false`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_STRUCTURED_OUTPUT_IN_PROMPT=false
# LiteLLM/Bedrock: mark the prompt for the provider's prompt cache. Unset = on for models
# named "claude"; set true for a Claude model behind an ARN or alias, false to turn it off.
# Use the provider's prompt cache on the LiteLLM-backed providers (`litellm`, `litellmrouter`, `bedrock`): mark the
# prompt where the cache should end, and keep one reply shape across a reflect's turns so each turn reads the earlier
# ones back from the cache. It applies to every LLM call those providers make (retain, consolidation, reflect): each
# one marks its system prompt, and reflect, the only multi-turn tool conversation, also gets the shared reply shape,
# which is where the savings come from. It is one switch for every LiteLLM-backed model at once: set `true` for a
# Claude ARN on reflect and a Nova retain model gets the markers too. The direct `anthropic` provider always caches
# and ignores this, and `HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_PROMPT_CACHE_ENABLED` (Gemini's explicit cache) does not turn it off.
# Leave unset and it is on for a model whose name contains `claude`. Set `true` for a Claude model whose name does
# not say so, such as a Bedrock application inference profile ARN or a proxy alias; set `false` to turn it off.
# Measured on Bedrock Haiku 4.5: a reflect's input cost dropped about 50%. Turning it on for other models is not
# recommended: on Bedrock, Nova wrote more to the cache than it read back, Mistral and Llama made extra calls, and
# Kimi rejects the cache marker.
# 默认（官方文档）：Model name decides；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_LITELLM_PROMPT_CACHE=

# Transport-level output cap for reflect's final synthesis call. Unset = uncapped:
# the model runs to a natural stop and the reflect/mental-model max_tokens governs
# visible length via a prompt directive + a post-hoc rewrite (not by truncating the
# provider call, which on thinking models is eaten by reasoning tokens and cuts pages
# off mid-word). Set an integer only to enforce a hard cost ceiling on the call.
# Transport-level output cap (`max_completion_tokens`) for reflect's final synthesis call. Unset means uncapped: the
# model runs to a natural stop and the reflect/mental-model `max_tokens` governs *visible* length via a prompt
# directive plus a post-hoc rewrite, not by truncating the provider call. On thinking models the raw provider budget
# is consumed by reasoning tokens, so a hard cap here would cut pages off mid-word. Set an integer only to enforce a
# hard cost ceiling on the synthesis call. When set, the same cap applies to every reflect loop turn; when unset, a
# loop turn that only picks the next search is capped at 1024 tokens.
# 默认（官方文档）：Unset (uncapped)；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_REFLECT_MAX_COMPLETION_TOKENS=16000

# Diagnostic: on any LLM 4xx, log the exact assembled request ([LLM_4XX_DUMP]) --
# serialized request config (message bodies stripped) + capped per-message previews.
# For debugging otherwise-unreproducible rejected calls. Off by default.
# Diagnostic: when enabled, on any LLM `4xx` the provider logs `[LLM_4XX_DUMP]` with the request as actually
# assembled — the serialized request config (response schema + generation params, message bodies stripped) and
# length-capped per-message previews — so an otherwise-unreproducible rejected request can be inspected. Wired into
# all remote providers (Gemini/Vertex, OpenAI-compatible incl. Fireworks/Nous, Anthropic, LiteLLM incl. Router,
# Codex). Off by default; leave off in normal operation.
# 默认（官方文档）：`false`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_DEBUG_DUMP_4XX=false

# Example: Anthropic Claude configuration
# Provider: `openai`, `openai-responses`, `openai-codex`, `chatgpt`, `claude-code`, `cursor`, `antigravity`,
# `github-copilot`, `anthropic`, `gemini`, `groq`, `minimax`, `deepseek`, `zai`, `opencode-go`, `meta`, `nous`,
# `xai-oauth`, `fireworks`, `ollama`, `ollama-cloud`, `lmstudio`, `llamacpp`, `vertexai`, `bedrock`, `litellm`,
# `litellmrouter`, `volcano`, `openrouter`, `requesty`, `none`, or `package.module:ClassName` for a [custom
# provider](./extensions.md#custom-llm-provider)
# 默认（官方文档）：`openai`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# API key for providers that require one; unused by `github-copilot`. Optional for `anthropic` when [Workload
# Identity Federation](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/manage-claude/workload-identity-federation) is configured
# (see the Anthropic example below)
# 默认（官方文档）：-；下一行为上游示例值。
# 安全：敏感凭证占位符；请替换并保护 .env，勿提交或公开。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_API_KEY=your-anthropic-api-key
# Model name
# 默认（官方文档）：`gpt-5-mini`；下一行为上游示例值。
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-20250514

# Example: GitHub Copilot subscription via the official Copilot SDK
# Sign in with Copilot CLI first; no HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_API_KEY is needed.
# Provider: `openai`, `openai-responses`, `openai-codex`, `chatgpt`, `claude-code`, `cursor`, `antigravity`,
